tutuaword License Overview
==========================

Copyright (c) 2026 Amit Kumar

This repository is licensed in three parts. Which license applies to a file
depends on where that file lives.

  Component      Paths                                    License
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Core Engine    crates/, app/, docs/, scripts/,          MPL 2.0
                 fixtures/, and all other files not
                 listed below
  Plugins        plugins/                                 Apache License 2.0
  SDK            sdk/                                     MIT License

Full texts:

  MPL 2.0             LICENSE-MPL-2.0
  Apache License 2.0  LICENSE-APACHE-2.0
  MIT License         LICENSE-MIT


Core Engine — Mozilla Public License 2.0
----------------------------------------

Covers the Rust workspace under crates/ (the document model, editing engine,
text shaping, layout, rendering, file-format handlers, the FFI and WASM
bridges, and the plugin host), the Flutter application under app/, and the
supporting documentation and tooling.

The MPL is a file-level copyleft. You may combine this code with proprietary
code in a larger work, and that larger work may be released under terms of
your choosing. If you modify a file that is covered by the MPL, that file
must remain under the MPL and its source must be made available to the
recipients of your distribution.

As permitted by Section 3.1 of the MPL, this notice stands in place of a
per-file header. Every file in the paths listed above is Covered Software
under the MPL 2.0 unless it carries a different license notice of its own.


Plugins — Apache License 2.0
----------------------------

Covers plugin implementations under plugins/, including first-party plugins
distributed through the marketplace.

Apache 2.0 is permissive and carries an explicit patent grant, so plugin
authors can build on and redistribute this code without the file-level
copyleft that applies to the engine.


SDK — MIT License
-----------------

Covers the plugin developer SDK under sdk/: type definitions, the manifest
schema and validator, the local development server, the test harness, and the
publishing CLI, across their Rust, Python, and JavaScript distributions.

MIT is the least restrictive of the three, so that depending on the SDK
imposes essentially no obligations on the plugins people write with it.


Notes
-----

The plugins/ and sdk/ directories are planned for Phase 6 and do not exist
yet. Their licenses are declared here in advance so the boundary is fixed
before the code is written.

Third-party dependencies are covered by their own licenses. See the
dependency manifests (Cargo.toml, pubspec.yaml) for the full list.
